---
import PhotographyLayout from '../../layouts/PhotographyLayout.astro';

const partOne = [
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_2.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_3.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_4.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_5.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_1.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/1_6.jpg"
];
const partTwo = [
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_1.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_2.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_3.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_4.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_5.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/2_6.jpg"
];
const partThree = [
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_1.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_2.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_3.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_4.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_5.jpg",
    "/image/Photography/Automonument/3_6.jpg"
];
---

<PhotographyLayout
    title={"Automonument"}
    subtitle={"Photography | Hong Kong"}
    ogDescription={"A photography series inspired by Rem Koolhaas's theory of the Automonument, capturing Hong Kong skyscrapers as monumental urban presences."}
    image={"https://xdd44.xyz/image/Photography/Automonument/1_2.jpg"}
>
    <div class="container">
        <p style="padding-top: 12vh;">
            &quot;Beyond a certain critical mass each structure becomes a monument, or at least raises that expectation through its size alone, even if the sum or the nature of the individual activities it accommodates does not deserve a monumental expression
        </p>
        <p>
            ...
        </p>
        <p>
            This monument of the 20th century is the <i>Automonument</i>, and its purest manifestation is the Skyscraper.&quot;
        </p>
        <br>
        <br>
        <br>
        <br>
        <br>
        <p>-- Rem Koolhaas, &quot;The Frontier in the Sky,&quot; in <i>Delirious New York</i> --</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
        <p style="padding-top: 20vh;">
            Although Rem Koolhaas proposed &quot;Theory of Bigness&quot; two decades ago based on his observation of Manhattan, I can feel the effect of &quot;Automonument&quot; everywhere in Hong Kong. Even more, the density and variety of buildings here seem to
            generate their unique interpretation. Thus, though this series, I'd like to capture these &quot;Automonuments&quot; with my own camera and understanding.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
        <h3 style="padding-top: 17.5vh;">
            I
        </h3>
        <br>
        <br>
        <p>
            &quot;Beyond a certain scale...&quot;
        </p>
    </div>
    {partOne.map(src => (
        <div class="container">
            <img src={src} />
        </div>
    ))}

    <div class="container">
        <h3 style="padding-top: 17.5vh;">
            II
        </h3>
        <br>
        <br>
        <p>
            &quot;The façade can no longer reveal...&quot;
        </p>
    </div>
    {partTwo.map(src => (
        <div class="container">
            <img src={src} />
        </div>
    ))}

    <div class="container">
        <h3 style="padding-top: 17.5vh;">
            III
        </h3>
        <br>
        <br>
        <p>
            &quot;It coexists...&quot;
        </p>
    </div>
    {partThree.map(src => (
        <div class="container">
            <img src={src} />
        </div>
    ))}
</PhotographyLayout>
